---
description: Isolate user data, and do not shame people for changed goals.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Product boundaries

- Scope every user-owned read and write to the authenticated user.
- Verify Google ID tokens on the server. Never accept a client-supplied user id or email as identity.
- Do not log tokens, secrets, letter text, personal notes, or presigned URLs.
- Do not send personal content to ads, analytics, crash reports, or URLs.
- Do not invent credentials, store identifiers, legal text, or support contacts.
- Overdue, abandoned, or changed goals stay valid. Do not use shame, guilt, or failure language. Do not predict a user's death. Expected lifespan is optional and user-provided.
